    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-11T09:20:33+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-11T09:20:33+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-10T22:50:33Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-10T22:50:33Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A weak ridge of high pressure develops south of Bight today. This ridge will persist into Thursday before a broad area of low pressure develops over SA on Friday. This low will track eastwards, making way for a new high pressure ridge in the west on Saturday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-11T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-12T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-10T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-11T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Winds southerly 25 to 40 km/h decreasing to 15 to 25 km/h in the late evening. Daytime maximum temperatures 29 to 37.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">High</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:00am to 5:00pm, UV Index predicted to reach 11 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-12T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-13T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-11T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-12T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower north of Leigh Creek, most likely in the late afternoon and evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Leigh Creek in the late afternoon and evening. Winds south to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northeast to southeasterly in the morning then tending southeast to southwesterly in the early afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 13 and 24 with daytime temperatures reaching 32 to 39.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-13T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-14T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-12T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-13T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers south of Yunta, medium chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h during the morning then tending northwest to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 19 and 25 with daytime temperatures reaching 33 to 40.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-14T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-15T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-13T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-14T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower in the far northeast, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning and afternoon. Winds south to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 17 and 25 with daytime temperatures reaching 30 to 39.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
